# Utilizing Module

The `utilizing` module provides generic, domain-agnostic value types and helpers
shared across the entire library. Nothing in this module should import from
`coring`, `backending`, or `frontending`.

Class diagram: [utilizing.puml](utilizing.puml)

---

## File map

```
src/yasched/utilizing/
  GenericSingleton.py      # singleton mixin base class
  GenericRegistry.py       # generic string-keyed registry
  Color.py                 # immutable RGBA color value
  ColorRegistry.py         # named-color registry (plain class)
  SingletonColorRegistry.py # singleton wrapper around ColorRegistry
  Date.py                  # calendar date with flexible parsing
  Time.py                  # time-of-day with flexible parsing
  Duration.py              # time duration with flexible parsing
```

---

## Classes

| Class                    | Design doc                                               | Purpose                                        |
|--------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| `GenericSingleton`       | [GenericSingleton.dsg](GenericSingleton.dsg)             | Mixin that enforces a single instance          |
| `GenericRegistry`        | [GenericRegistry.dsg](GenericRegistry.dsg)               | String-keyed registry with alias support       |
| `Color`                  | [Color.dsg](Color.dsg)                                   | Immutable RGBA color value                     |
| `ColorRegistry`          | [ColorRegistry.dsg](ColorRegistry.dsg)                   | Registry of named colors (plain class)         |
| `SingletonColorRegistry` | [SingletonColorRegistry.dsg](SingletonColorRegistry.dsg) | Process-wide singleton color registry          |
| `Date`                   | [Date.dsg](Date.dsg)                                     | Calendar date with multi-format parsing        |
| `Time`                   | [Time.dsg](Time.dsg)                                     | Time-of-day with multi-format parsing          |
| `Duration`               | [Duration.dsg](Duration.dsg)                             | Time span with human-readable parsing          |

---

## Design rules for this module

- All classes are immutable value objects (frozen dataclasses) unless stated otherwise.
- Parsing always validates and raises `ValueError` on bad input.
- Each class stores its value in exactly one canonical internal representation.
- `Date`, `Time`, and `Duration` wrap their corresponding `datetime` stdlib types
  (`datetime.date`, `datetime.time`, `datetime.timedelta`) rather than reimplementing
  time arithmetic.
